**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests`

**How to implement.** A study opens a material version into a working copy whose every component is a parameter, generated from the material's crystal record, shared by every sample made of it (001 §I 'Material parameters as unknowns: a study OPENS a material version, which creates a study-local working copy, stored in the study file, with `Unknown` components; every sample made of it shares them (`MaterialScope`)'; 001 §N 'Parameter-axis generation: … publishes its `ParameterAxis` list. Case 1b's generated axes equal `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes` — an exact test'; 001 §P `OpenMaterial`; the S11.1 brief 'Generated axes', 'the EXACT test'; .spec-md §3.16 'its generated axes are that record's `axes`'). A complexity tree publishes no parameter axis in this spec: its eps is formula, table or constant data the ladder edits, so a material is fitted through its crystal-parameter form (step 355). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. In `Studies.fs`, after step 360's member: (1) `type ParameterAxis<'Parameters> with member this.parameterValueOf (p : 'Parameters) : ParameterValue` (`this.read p` as a `ParameterValue`, the one conversion from an axis read to a parameter's number) and `member this.writeValue (value : ParameterValue) (p : 'Parameters) : 'Parameters` (`this.write value.value p`, the one conversion back). (2) `type CrystalParameters with member this.parameterAxes : ParameterAxis<CrystalParameters> list`: the axes of its record (`UniaxialParameters.axes`, `TriclinicParameters.axes` or `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes`, step 353) in their order, each lifted onto the crystal by a private helper per case: the same `name` and the same field case (`RefractionIndexField`, `RhoValueField`, `EpsValueField`), its access reading the record of a crystal of the same case and writing back a crystal of that case; a crystal of another case reads as `this` reads and is written back unchanged, because the axes are generated from `this` and a study applies them to its own working copy only. The list is generated, never hand-written. (3) On `OpenedMaterial` (step 358): `static member openFrom (version : MaterialVersionId) (entry : MaterialEntry) : Result<OpenedMaterial, StudyError>`, for a `CrystalParameterPhysics crystal` the working copy `{ version; name = entry.name; crystal; parameters }` whose parameters are, per generated axis in order, `{ name = axis.name; state = KnownParameter (axis.parameterValueOf crystal) }`, and for a `ComplexityPhysics` `MaterialWithoutParametersErr` naming the entry; `member this.withParameterState (name : ParameterName) (state : ParameterState) : Result<OpenedMaterial, StudyError>`, `UnknownStudyParameterErr` naming the material and the name when no component has it, `InvalidStudyParameterErr` carrying the `ItemError.describe` of `{ name = name; state = state }.validate` (step 214) when the state breaks its rules, and otherwise that component's state replaced in place (freeing a component is its `UnknownParameter` state, 001 §I); and `member this.currentCrystal : CrystalParameters`, the crystal with each component written through its generated axis at its parameter's current number (a known or calibrated value, an unknown's start), in order. (4) On `Study`: `member this.openMaterial (version : MaterialVersionId) (entry : MaterialEntry) : Result<Study, StudyError>`, `MaterialAlreadyOpenErr` naming the version when `materials` holds it, `openFrom`'s error passing through, and otherwise the study with the working copy appended; `member this.withMaterialParameterState (version : MaterialVersionId) (name : ParameterName) (state : ParameterState) : Result<Study, StudyError>`, `UnknownStudyMaterialErr` naming the version when it is not opened, and otherwise its copy's `withParameterState` in place. (5) `type Sample with member this.openedMaterialsIn (study : Study) : OpenedMaterial list`: the study's working copies whose version the sample's `structure.referencedMaterialVersions` (step 61) holds, in study order, so every sample made of an opened material reads the same copy (`MaterialScope`); the forward model reads it (S11.2). `StudyError` gains `MaterialWithoutParametersErr` (`the material publishes no parameter to fit: <reason>`), `MaterialAlreadyOpenErr` (`the study already opens that material version: <reason>`), `UnknownStudyMaterialErr` (`the study opens no such material version: <reason>`), `UnknownStudyParameterErr` (`the study has no such parameter: <reason>`) and `InvalidStudyParameterErr` (`the parameter state is not valid: <reason>`). No cache, conversion or other member is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs`, `module StudyMaterialTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, over test-local entries of each crystal case (fifteen distinct literal values for the absorbing probe) and a test-local `MaterialVersionId`: `the generated axes of an opened absorbing triclinic material equal AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes` (the exact test): the opened copy's `crystal.parameterAxes` has the fifteen names of `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes` in its order and the same field case at each position; at each position the generated read of `AbsorbingTriclinicCrystal probe` equals the record axis's read of `probe` exactly, and the generated write of 2.5 times that value answers `AbsorbingTriclinicCrystal` of the record axis's write of it; and the copy's parameters are those fifteen names, each `KnownParameter` at the probe's value; `an opened uniaxial or triclinic material generates its record's axes the same way`: the same over a uniaxial (4 axes) and a triclinic (9) entry; `a material whose physics is a complexity tree, or one opened twice, is refused`: a constant isotropic complexity entry answers `MaterialWithoutParametersErr`, and opening the absorbing version twice `MaterialAlreadyOpenErr`; `freeing a component makes it an unknown in place, and the working copy's crystal reads each parameter's current value`: setting `n3` to an `UnknownParameter` starting at 1.70 within [1.60, 1.80] changes that parameter in place, the copy's `currentCrystal` reading index3 1.70 and every other field the probe's; a name the copy lacks answers `UnknownStudyParameterErr` and reversed bounds `InvalidStudyParameterErr`, the study unchanged; `every sample made of an opened material shares its working copy`: a plate sample whose substrate is the opened version and a film sample whose `Repeated` cell names it each answer [the copy], and a sample of another version answers []. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the five new cases.

**Acceptance.** After OpenMaterial's pure half lands, `OpenedMaterial.openFrom` MUST turn a crystal-parameter version into a working copy whose parameters follow the record's generated axes, refusing a complexity tree, and the generated axes of an opened `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters` material MUST equal `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes` in names, order, field kinds and read / write on a probe; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the generated axes of an opened absorbing triclinic material equal AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes`, `an opened uniaxial or triclinic material generates its record's axes the same way`, `a material whose physics is a complexity tree, or one opened twice, is refused`, `freeing a component makes it an unknown in place, and the working copy's crystal reads each parameter's current value` and `every sample made of an opened material shares its working copy`, the count rising by 5, and the widened `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.
